  priceLabel: 'Chimpanzee permit USD 100 / person',
  priceNote: 'Canopy Walk USD 60. Colobus trekking USD 60. All-inclusive packages from USD 400.',
  intro: [
    'Nyungwe Forest National Park in southwestern Rwanda is one of Africa\'s most ancient and biodiverse montane rainforests. Dating back over 100,000 years, the 1,019 km- forest has never been entirely covered by ice and has served as a refuge for plants and animals through successive climate cycles, resulting in extraordinary levels of endemism.',
    'The park is Rwanda\'s premier primate destination outside the gorilla parks. Thirteen chimpanzee communities and 13 other primate species live in the forest, including troops of Angola colobus monkeys numbering over 400 individuals - the largest such troops in Africa. The colobus troops are habituated and can be approached on foot with guided walks.',
